1658
01:03:40.818 --> 01:03:43.845
Certainly those are businesses that should be separated,

1659
01:03:43.845 --> 01:03:47.577
but Google is not gonna voluntarily cut ties with YouTube

1660
01:03:47.577 --> 01:03:48.785
and spin it off.

1661
01:03:48.785 --> 01:03:51.027
But if they were smart,

1662
01:03:51.027 --> 01:03:53.314
if you listen to what Scott's saying,

1663
01:03:53.314 --> 01:03:57.722
they would spin off their cloud service, right?

1664
01:03:57.722 --> 01:04:00.701
Like, let go of Drive to say,

1665
01:04:00.701 --> 01:04:04.025
we're a good actor in the space don't go after us.

1666
01:04:04.025 --> 01:04:04.858
Yeah.

1667
01:04:04.858 --> 01:04:07.080
So they can hold onto YouTube, right?

1668
01:04:07.080 --> 01:04:08.246
You know what I mean?

1669
01:04:08.246 --> 01:04:11.992
Like, it's gonna be fascinating to see the kind of jockeying

1670
01:04:11.992 --> 01:04:13.735
and the strategy and the moves that these companies

1671
01:04:13.735 --> 01:04:14.568
are gonna make.

1672
01:04:14.568 --> 01:04:17.671
But I think breaking them up will be this amazing spark

1673
01:04:17.671 --> 01:04:19.558
to innovation in the space.

1674
01:04:19.558 --> 01:04:21.611
And I think consumers will benefit from that.

1675
01:04:21.611 --> 01:04:22.619
So you think it's gonna happen?

1676
01:04:22.619 --> 01:04:24.866
Well, the lawsuits are moving forward.

1677
01:04:24.866 --> 01:04:25.699
Right.

1678
01:04:25.699 --> 01:04:27.471
How they'll play out is anybody's guess.

1679
01:04:27.471 --> 01:04:30.236
But I do think it's interesting that this is happening right

1680
01:04:30.236 --> 01:04:31.761
at the end of the Trump administration,

1681
01:04:31.761 --> 01:04:33.288
as we're heading into Biden.

1682
01:04:33.288 --> 01:04:35.208
Certainly the Biden administration

1683
01:04:35.208 --> 01:04:39.625
is gonna be much more politically interested in this.

1684
01:04:42.248 --> 01:04:45.331
Although Trump, he was on record as saying,

1685
01:04:45.331 --> 01:04:48.259
these companies are too big and seem to have an interest in.

1686
01:04:48.259 --> 01:04:49.092
Yeah.

1687
01:04:49.092 --> 01:04:52.484
Ultimately these just spark people bring these suits.

1688
01:04:52.484 --> 01:04:55.982
They aren't really political appointees there.

1689
01:04:55.982 --> 01:04:58.528
No, but if you're a DOJ,

1690
01:04:58.528 --> 01:04:59.695
if you're the attorney general,

1691
01:04:59.695 --> 01:05:03.226
you're still taking orders from The White House

1692
01:05:03.226 --> 01:05:04.506
in terms of the kind of cases

1693
01:05:04.506 --> 01:05:06.200
that they want you to pursue or not pursue.

1694
01:05:06.200 --> 01:05:09.053
It's interesting when it comes to consumers,

1695
01:05:09.053 --> 01:05:11.622
when you having seen social dilemma

1696
01:05:11.622 --> 01:05:12.704
and we've talked about it,

1697
01:05:12.704 --> 01:05:15.255
is like, who are the consumers of Facebook

1698
01:05:15.255 --> 01:05:16.552
and Google and YouTube?

1699
