that now was a period of great innovation

1735
01:06:32.589 --> 01:06:33.647
as a result of that.

1736
01:06:33.647 --> 01:06:35.127
And I think that's what you'll see here now,

1737
01:06:35.127 --> 01:06:38.490
in terms of the moves that these companies are making,

1738
01:06:38.490 --> 01:06:41.245
what should they do prophylactically?

1739
01:06:41.245 --> 01:06:44.331
How are they trying to protect themselves right now?

1740
01:06:44.331 --> 01:06:49.207
You see Facebook starting to take their messaging service

1741
01:06:49.207 --> 01:06:52.650
and integrated across all of their platforms.

1742
01:06:52.650 --> 01:06:54.968
So it becomes very difficult to disentangle.

1743
01:06:54.968 --> 01:06:59.801
Whereas Apple conversely is cutting its commission charges

1744
01:07:00.844 --> 01:07:03.039
on the App Store to say, we're a good actor.

1745
01:07:03.039 --> 01:07:04.618
Like I think what Tim Cook is doing

1746
01:07:04.618 --> 01:07:06.606
and how Apple is proceeding here,

1747
01:07:06.606 --> 01:07:09.727
of all of these, they're in the best stead

1748
01:07:09.727 --> 01:07:13.454
in terms of weathering this and not being a big target,

1749
01:07:13.454 --> 01:07:16.325
but when Facebook is going out of its way

1750
01:07:16.325 --> 01:07:18.575
to make separating WhatsApp

1751
01:07:20.636 --> 01:07:23.596
from the rest of its ecosystem more difficult

1752
01:07:23.596 --> 01:07:28.596
to me that makes them all the more likely hard targets.

1753
01:07:28.946 --> 01:07:30.427
Well, also Apple can afford it

1754
01:07:30.427 --> 01:07:31.900
'cause their big money is the phone.

1755
01:07:31.900 --> 01:07:32.900
It's the hardware,

1756
01:07:32.900 --> 01:07:34.952
that's where they're making their coin.

1757
01:07:34.952 --> 01:07:35.785
Right.

1758
01:07:35.785 --> 01:07:36.846
It's different kind of thing,

1759
01:07:36.846 --> 01:07:39.096
but they're so massive too,

1760
01:07:40.211 --> 01:07:43.616
that the lens is gonna get aimed in their direction

1761
01:07:43.616 --> 01:07:44.823
at some point.

1762
01:07:44.823 --> 01:07:48.053
But this idea of who's the customer,

1763
01:07:48.053 --> 01:07:49.159
is super interesting.

1764
01:07:49.159 --> 01:07:49.992
Yeah.

1765
01:07:49.992 --> 01:07:51.242
Like the advertisers are the customer,

1766
01:07:51.242 --> 01:07:52.491
that's how they make their money.

1767
01:07:52.491 --> 01:07:53.836
So they gotta keep them happy.

1768
01:07:53.836 --> 01:07:55.908
And that's what comes out of this.

1769
01:07:55.908 --> 01:07:58.260
Like, who's the consumer?

1770
01:07:58.260 --> 01:07:59.838
'Cause people are gonna,

1771
01:07:59.838 --> 01:08:01.741
the news is gonna be reported and consumers

1772
01:08:01.741 --> 01:08:02.771
is gonna be used a lot.

1773
01:08:02.771 --> 01:08:05.138
And I hope that what we're paying attention to,

1774
01:08:05.138 --> 01:08:08.996
is I wanna know who Facebook thinks the consumer is.

1775
01:08:08.996 --> 01:08:12.308
Well, I think we know that Facebook thinks

1776
01:08:12.308 --> 01:08:15.545
the consumer is the advertiser.

1777
01:08:15.545 --> 01:08:16.834
But what do they call them?

1778
01:08:16.834 --> 01:08:17.667
But what is gonna get reported

1779
01:08:17.667 --> 01:08:20.165
and how is the narrative gonna be spot?

1780
01:08:20.165 --> 01:08:24.755
I think that with the exception of very savvy reporters

1781
01:08:24.755 --> 01:08:27.172
like Kevin Reus and the like,

1782
01:08:28.348 --> 01:08:33.348
most of it's gonna get positioned as us being the consumer.

1783
01:08:33.508 --> 01:08:34.341
Yeah.

1784
01:08:34.341 --> 01:08:35.174
Don't you think?

1785
01:08:35.174 --> 01:08:36.007
I think so.

1786
01:08:36.007 --> 01:08:37.230
I think user and consumer are two different things

1787
01:08:37.230 --> 01:08:40.622
in this case and often they're not.

1788
01:08:40.622 --> 01:08:42.861
So like that's, that was always the argument

1789
01:08:42.861 --> 01:08:45.173
for don't break up Amazon

1790
01:08:45.173 --> 01:08:46.671
when they were getting all their terrible press

1791
01:08:46.671 --> 01:08:48.425
for how they operated their business

1792
01:08:48.425 --> 01:08:51.025
and abusive employee abuse and whatever,

1793
01:08:51.025 --> 01:08:53.340
was that you can say what you want,

1794
01:08:53.340 --> 01:08:57.070
but the consumer gets lower prices.

1795
01:08:57.070 --> 01:08:58.257
That's what they tricky, right?

1796
01:08:58.257 --> 01:08:59.607
Is the dipper company out of business,

1797
01:08:59.607 --> 01:09:01.367
but the consumer gets lower prices.

1798
01:09:01.367 --> 01:09:02.938
They chased that company out of business.

1799
01:09:02.938 --> 01:09:05.729
Walmart cracks down on Mom-and-pop shops

1800
01:09:05.729 --> 01:09:07.110
all over small town America,

1801
01:09:07.110 --> 01:09:09.020
but the consumer gets a lower prices.

1802
01:09:09.020 --> 01:09:12.819
But the problem is when you look at things just like that,

1803
01:09:12.819 --> 01:09:15.413
the collateral damage is completely ignored

1804
01:09:15.413 --> 01:09:18.120
and you would need to buy things so cheap

1805
01:09:18.120 --> 01:09:20.322
if everyone made a little more money, right?

1806
01:09:20.322 --> 01:09:22.883
If the wealth was shared a bit more.

1807
01:09:22.883 --> 01:09:24.886
And that's the biggest problem with tech companies

1808
01:09:24.886 --> 01:09:28.436
is they siphoned money into smaller and smaller straws

1809
01:09:28.436 --> 01:09:31.189
or big straws, but for few people.

1810
01:09:31.189 --> 01:09:32.022
Yeah.

1811
01:09:32.022 --> 01:09:33.671
And that's why I think breaking them up

1812
01:09:33.671 --> 01:09:36.131
and having more competition means

1813
01:09:36.131 --> 01:09:38.431
more money gets spread around.

1814
01:09:38.431 --> 01:09:40.843
And I think that that's not being talked about really,

1815
01:09:40.843 --> 01:09:42.023
but that's what it's about.

1816
01:09:42.023 --> 01:09:46.966
It's a way to redistribute wealth in an era of a Gilda age.

1817
01:09:46.966 --> 01:09:47.799
Yeah.

1818
01:09:47.799 --> 01:09:51.491
Facebook's argument is there is a robust market

1819
01:09:51.491 --> 01:09:53.528
when it comes to social networks

1820
01:09:53.528 --> 01:09:55.898
and there is a lot of competition when you look at Tik Tok

1821
01:09:55.898 --> 01:09:57.571
and Snap and things like that.

1822
01:09:57.571 --> 01:09:59.505
But is there really?

1823
01:09:59.505 --> 01:10:01.404
Who looks at Tik Tok, Rich?

1824
01:10:01.404 --> 01:10:03.862
(laughing)

1825
01:10:03.862 --> 01:10:05.191
Tik Tok is huge.

1826
01:10:05.191 --> 01:10:06.024
I know it's huge.

1827
01:10:06.024 --> 01:10:07.191
I can't do it.

1828
01:10:08.137 --> 01:10:10.018
That's the bridge too far for me.

1829
01:10:10.018 --> 01:10:12.895
My daughters are on it all the time.

1830
01:10:12.895 --> 01:10:13.728
I'm sure.

1831
01:10:13.728 --> 01:10:16.290
I just, that's where I have to draw the line and say,

1832
01:10:16.290 --> 01:10:18.546
okay, it's not appropriate.

1833
01:10:18.546 --> 01:10:20.060
Maybe I'm just getting older.

1834
01:10:20.060 --> 01:10:21.489
I'm listening to the Obama Book.

1835
01:10:21.489 --> 01:10:22.933
That's what I'm doing for your talent.

1836
01:10:22.933 --> 01:10:23.766
How is it?

1837
01:10:23.766 --> 01:10:24.599
It's fabulous.

1838
01:10:24.599 --> 01:10:25.432
Yeah.

1839
01:10:25.432 --> 01:10:26.265
I'm sure it is.

1840
01:10:26.265 --> 01:10:28.415
Him and his little book out there.

1841
01:10:28.415 --> 01:10:29.248
(laughing)

1842
01:10:29.248 --> 01:10:32.481
Dainty little 750 page volume one.

1843
01:10:32.481 --> 01:10:33.314
All right.

1844
01:10:33.314 --> 01:10:34.771
Well, more will be revealed on this.

1845
01:10:34.771 --> 01:10:37.061
And I think that concludes this week's edition

1846
01:10:37.061 --> 01:10:38.211
of legal corner.

1847
01:10:38.211 --> 01:10:39.044
(laughing)

1848
01:10:39.044 --> 01:10:40.181
Slash teachable moment.

1849
01:10:40.181 --> 01:10:41.014
Yeah.

1850
01:10:41.014 --> 01:10:41.847
I hope you learned something kids.

1851
01:10:41.847 --> 01:10:43.058
What do we got next?

1852
