2902
01:49:42.042 --> 01:49:43.635
(laughing)

2903
01:49:43.635 --> 01:49:45.573
But I don't mean that in like, beware,

2904
01:49:45.573 --> 01:49:46.549
what I mean is that,

2905
01:49:46.549 --> 01:49:48.935
it doesn't have to be in a negative way.

2906
01:49:48.935 --> 01:49:51.935
It can be in like you feel so at one

2907
01:49:53.784 --> 01:49:54.850
with the cosmos some days,

2908
01:49:54.850 --> 01:49:57.590
that you feel like a speck.

2909
01:49:57.590 --> 01:49:58.423
Yeah.

2910
01:49:58.423 --> 01:50:00.978
And that is humbling in a way that's like, wow,

2911
01:50:00.978 --> 01:50:02.277
that's how big the world.

2912
01:50:02.277 --> 01:50:03.591
That's how beautiful the world is.

2913
01:50:03.591 --> 01:50:05.748
And I'm playing my little part.

2914
01:50:05.748 --> 01:50:08.438
And it could also be the other way which is,

2915
01:50:08.438 --> 01:50:10.512
you might get kicked in the face a couple of times

2916
01:50:10.512 --> 01:50:12.084
to see if you really wanna do this.

2917
01:50:12.084 --> 01:50:12.917
Right.

2918
01:50:12.917 --> 01:50:15.843
It is humbling innately to go on,

2919
01:50:15.843 --> 01:50:17.568
branch out on your own path

2920
01:50:17.568 --> 01:50:18.733
and try to do something

2921
01:50:18.733 --> 01:50:21.637
that you didn't know that you could do,

2922
01:50:21.637 --> 01:50:23.175
or that you just dared yourself to do.

2923
01:50:23.175 --> 01:50:26.098
It is a humbling act I think.

2924
01:50:26.098 --> 01:50:26.931
Right.

2925
01:50:26.931 --> 01:50:27.764
Rob Bell would.

2926
01:50:27.764 --> 01:50:30.031
So we're leaving Joe with this idea

2927
01:50:30.031 --> 01:50:33.282
that what he thinks his ego is actually humility.

2928
01:50:33.282 --> 01:50:37.321
And what he thinks is humility is actually ego and fear,

2929
01:50:37.321 --> 01:50:41.233
because he's attached to this story that actually is false.

2930
01:50:41.233 --> 01:50:42.066
Yeah.

2931
01:50:42.066 --> 01:50:43.543
Or that's certainly one way to look at it.

2932
01:50:43.543 --> 01:50:44.376
Right.

2933
01:50:44.376 --> 01:50:46.480
And if it gets you on the road to self actualizing,

2934
01:50:46.480 --> 01:50:47.451
then look at it that way.

2935
01:50:47.451 --> 01:50:48.284
Right.

2936
01:50:48.284 --> 01:50:51.907
And Joe, if this doesn't resonate with you at all, then.

2937
01:50:51.907 --> 01:50:52.740
You get your money back.

2938
01:50:52.740 --> 01:50:53.573
Yeah.

2939
01:50:53.573 --> 01:50:54.406
(laughing)

2940
01:50:54.406 --> 01:50:56.628
I'm refunding you because I don't know enough

2941
01:50:56.628 --> 01:50:57.614
about the story,

2942
01:50:57.614 --> 01:51:01.498
but I have a feeling we might be onto something there.

2943
01:51:01.498 --> 01:51:04.646
And Color is just so I'm trying this new thing

2944
01:51:04.646 --> 01:51:07.010
where if you are concise with your question,

2945
01:51:07.010 --> 01:51:09.798
it gives you a better chance.

2946
01:51:09.798 --> 01:51:10.835
That's the Skolnick algorithm.

2947
01:51:10.835 --> 01:51:13.786
If you wanna game the algorithm, keep it short.

2948
01:51:13.786 --> 01:51:15.489
keep it short and into the point.

2949
01:51:15.489 --> 01:51:18.071
And also just be really clear thinking

2950
01:51:18.071 --> 01:51:19.952
and it might help,

2951
01:51:19.952 --> 01:51:20.785
a lot of these.

2952
01:51:20.785 --> 01:51:22.075
You can tell, some people are reading

2953
01:51:22.075 --> 01:51:23.980
from a script they've written themselves,

2954
01:51:23.980 --> 01:51:26.104
and it's easier to answer a question

2955
01:51:26.104 --> 01:51:27.432
that's a little bit clear.

2956
01:51:27.432 --> 01:51:29.008
And even though that that was esoteric,

2957
01:51:29.008 --> 01:51:29.841
it still was clear.

2958
01:51:29.841 --> 01:51:31.969
He still had a very specific thing he was asking.

2959
01:51:31.969 --> 01:51:33.918
He made his way through the algorithm.

2960
01:51:33.918 --> 01:51:35.380
He made it through.

2961
01:51:35.380 --> 01:51:36.213
All right,

2962
01:51:36.213 --> 01:51:37.046
let's go to the Seth from Wisconsin.

2963
01:51:37.046 --> 01:51:38.629
Let's go to Seth.

2964
01:52:45.196 --> 01:52:46.164
Thank you, Seth.

2965
01:52:46.164 --> 01:52:47.673
Thanks, Seth.

2966
01:52:47.673 --> 01:52:50.613
Also coming to us from a very cold part of the world.

2967
01:52:50.613 --> 01:52:51.446
Yeah.

2968
01:52:51.446 --> 01:52:52.285
And it's a divorce question.

2969
01:52:52.285 --> 01:52:53.433
I love divorce questions.

2970
01:52:53.433 --> 01:52:54.266
You do?

2971
01:52:54.266 --> 01:52:55.099
Yeah.

2972
01:52:55.099 --> 01:52:55.932
Well, let me say this.

2973
01:52:55.932 --> 01:52:58.321
We're not divorce relationship question.

2974
01:52:58.321 --> 01:52:59.154
Right.

2975
01:52:59.154 --> 01:52:59.987
Yeah.

2976
01:52:59.987 --> 01:53:03.437
Poor self esteem and avoidance of discomfort

2977
01:53:03.437 --> 01:53:08.104
is like the perfect one, two combo that fuels isolation,

2978
01:53:10.334 --> 01:53:13.449
that keeps a lot of people stuck.

2979
01:53:13.449 --> 01:53:14.600
Get some stuck,

2980
01:53:14.600 --> 01:53:17.750
keeps them stuck and also is very effective

2981
01:53:17.750 --> 01:53:20.689
for keeping people at arms length that day, right?

2982
01:53:20.689 --> 01:53:22.921
Like if you don't feel great about yourself

2983
01:53:22.921 --> 01:53:27.805
and you're not comfortable with any kind of conflict

2984
01:53:27.805 --> 01:53:31.578
or doing anything outside your small little zone of comfort,

2985
01:53:31.578 --> 01:53:36.564
then you're unlikely to take any risks with other people.

2986
01:53:36.564 --> 01:53:38.040
And that's gonna keep you separated

2987
01:53:38.040 --> 01:53:40.479
from other human beings.

2988
01:53:40.479 --> 01:53:43.222
So when I hear those two qualities,

2989
01:53:43.222 --> 01:53:46.193
I think what's behind that combination.

2990
01:53:46.193 --> 01:53:51.193
And I hear somebody who feels like they don't have a voice,

2991
01:53:51.927 --> 01:53:53.820
or they're not entitled to have a voice

2992
01:53:53.820 --> 01:53:54.748
or to speak their truth.

2993
01:53:54.748 --> 01:53:58.830
Somebody who's afraid of letting anyone else know

2994
01:53:58.830 --> 01:54:00.223
who they really are.

2995
01:54:00.223 --> 01:54:02.367
And perhaps somebody who even feels undeserving

2996
01:54:02.367 --> 01:54:04.034
of love itself.

2997
01:54:04.034 --> 01:54:07.284
And I think the avoidance of discomfort

2998
01:54:08.862 --> 01:54:11.914
is rooted in the sense that if somebody really knew you,

2999
01:54:11.914 --> 01:54:14.451
if they truly understood you,

3000
01:54:14.451 --> 01:54:16.503
if they could see right into your soul,

3001
01:54:16.503 --> 01:54:18.453
that they would leave you, right?

3002
01:54:18.453 --> 01:54:21.036
That you're not worthy of love.

3003
01:54:24.810 --> 01:54:28.132
But I think what I would urge Seth to do is,

3004
01:54:28.132 --> 01:54:32.577
is to look at how these tendencies maybe contributed

3005
01:54:32.577 --> 01:54:37.005
or in some way led to the dissolving of the marriage.

3006
01:54:37.005 --> 01:54:42.005
Obviously we don't know anything about what happened there.

3007
01:54:42.135 --> 01:54:43.552
But those things,

3008
01:54:44.520 --> 01:54:47.488
that avoidance of discomfort that poor self-esteem,

3009
01:54:47.488 --> 01:54:49.941
those are ways that they're like coping mechanisms

3010
01:54:49.941 --> 01:54:51.849
to keep you safe, right?

3011
01:54:51.849 --> 01:54:56.461
And to prevent you from being in the position of being hurt.

3012
01:54:56.461 --> 01:54:58.045
It seems like he's figured that out.

3013
01:54:58.045 --> 01:54:59.601
Like that is what led to it.

3014
01:54:59.601 --> 01:55:02.062
Ultimately that manifests the very thing

3015
01:55:02.062 --> 01:55:03.244
that you're trying to avoid.

3016
01:55:03.244 --> 01:55:04.077
You get hurt.

3017
01:55:04.077 --> 01:55:05.377
Right?

3018
01:55:05.377 --> 01:55:09.344
So in truth, it's the vulnerability, it's the taking risks.

3019
01:55:09.344 --> 01:55:11.098
It's the willingness and the courage

3020
01:55:11.098 --> 01:55:13.265
to whether that discomfort

3021
01:55:14.294 --> 01:55:17.164
that ultimately creates the intimacy.

3022
01:55:17.164 --> 01:55:18.389
It's counterintuitive, right?

3023
01:55:18.389 --> 01:55:20.097
Like if I stay safe,

3024
01:55:20.097 --> 01:55:23.344
then I can be in this relationship

3025
01:55:23.344 --> 01:55:24.432
and I'm not gonna get left,

3026
01:55:24.432 --> 01:55:26.222
but you have to take the risk

3027
01:55:26.222 --> 01:55:30.186
to pave the road for intimacy that brings you closer.

3028
01:55:30.186 --> 01:55:33.466
So as uncomfortable and as counterintuitive as it is,

3029
01:55:33.466 --> 01:55:38.216
that's I think the growth arc for this person to embrace.

3030
01:55:39.442 --> 01:55:41.847
Vulnerability, meaning revealing your,

3031
01:55:41.847 --> 01:55:43.094
how you really truly feel.

3032
01:55:43.094 --> 01:55:46.091
Being willing to be honest with somebody else

3033
01:55:46.091 --> 01:55:49.871
about your insecurities or your poor self-esteem,

3034
01:55:49.871 --> 01:55:50.704
or what's bothering you,

3035
01:55:50.704 --> 01:55:55.704
and the willingness to have the uncomfortable conversations.

3036
01:55:56.580 --> 01:55:58.812
Understanding that they may lead to a conflict,

3037
01:55:58.812 --> 01:56:01.765
but it's only through that kind of tension

3038
01:56:01.765 --> 01:56:05.111
that you can come to a place of understanding and bonding.

3039
01:56:05.111 --> 01:56:06.015
Well, you have some suggestions

3040
01:56:06.015 --> 01:56:08.184
in terms of how to cultivate that.

3041
01:56:08.184 --> 01:56:09.017
Yeah.

3042
01:56:09.017 --> 01:56:09.850
A couple things.

3043
01:56:09.850 --> 01:56:12.250
I think some of them are super basic and elementary.

3044
01:56:12.250 --> 01:56:13.833
The first thing is,

3045
01:56:13.833 --> 01:56:15.381
if you're trying to create those bonds,

3046
01:56:15.381 --> 01:56:19.574
you've got to set aside time for conversation

3047
01:56:19.574 --> 01:56:21.764
and treat that as sacred rather than just saying,

3048
01:56:21.764 --> 01:56:23.987
well, the next time I see this person,

3049
01:56:23.987 --> 01:56:24.858
I'll try to do it.

3050
01:56:24.858 --> 01:56:27.802
Like if you establish it as a formal thing,

3051
01:56:27.802 --> 01:56:31.089
that's calendared and respected by both parties,

3052
01:56:31.089 --> 01:56:32.715
you're creating a crucible,

3053
01:56:32.715 --> 01:56:36.565
like an environment in which there's expectations

3054
01:56:36.565 --> 01:56:38.701
around that kind of thing transpiring.

3055
01:56:38.701 --> 01:56:42.540
So setting aside time is super important.

3056
01:56:42.540 --> 01:56:45.319
I know that it's scary if you're somebody

3057
01:56:45.319 --> 01:56:47.239
who is conflict avoidant

3058
01:56:47.239 --> 01:56:50.322
or afraid of that kind of discomfort.

3059
01:56:51.590 --> 01:56:54.240
So the best way to get over that

3060
01:56:54.240 --> 01:56:58.032
is to start to practice it in a low stakes environment.

3061
01:56:58.032 --> 01:57:00.012
So maybe not with your ex-wife,

3062
01:57:00.012 --> 01:57:02.709
but find a friend who you trust

3063
01:57:02.709 --> 01:57:05.209
and use them as an experiment,

3064
01:57:06.582 --> 01:57:08.480
like say something vulnerable,

3065
01:57:08.480 --> 01:57:11.279
like take a risk and try to have a conversation

3066
01:57:11.279 --> 01:57:16.279
that shakes you out of that safety zone a little bit,

3067
01:57:16.358 --> 01:57:19.535
knowing that that person is somebody who's close to you

3068
01:57:19.535 --> 01:57:21.554
and nothing bad is gonna happen.

3069
01:57:21.554 --> 01:57:23.868
And I think that will help you acclimate

3070
01:57:23.868 --> 01:57:25.901
or get a sense of how this can work.

3071
01:57:25.901 --> 01:57:27.461
And then over time,

3072
01:57:27.461 --> 01:57:29.854
slowly increase the intensity,

3073
01:57:29.854 --> 01:57:32.003
take little, bigger and bigger risks

3074
01:57:32.003 --> 01:57:35.167
until you're ready to kind of do this with your ex-wife.

3075
01:57:35.167 --> 01:57:37.697
I wouldn't do the trial run with the ex-wife

3076
01:57:37.697 --> 01:57:42.256
because my sense is that that might be too perilous

3077
01:57:42.256 --> 01:57:43.126
at this moment.

3078
01:57:43.126 --> 01:57:46.128
You can do pushups to get ready for something like that.

3079
01:57:46.128 --> 01:57:48.690
Or even if it's for a new relationship,

3080
01:57:48.690 --> 01:57:50.795
which it could be for,

3081
01:57:50.795 --> 01:57:52.362
think of these things,

3082
01:57:52.362 --> 01:57:55.820
it's still good to get the muscle working with a friend

3083
01:57:55.820 --> 01:57:58.379
so that when the next relationship comes around,

3084
01:57:58.379 --> 01:58:00.603
that you're ready to be who you are.

3085
01:58:00.603 --> 01:58:01.436
Right.

3086
01:58:01.436 --> 01:58:03.749
And what a burden you're carrying around,

3087
01:58:03.749 --> 01:58:05.644
trying to prevent that person

3088
01:58:05.644 --> 01:58:07.540
from seeing who you really are,

3089
01:58:07.540 --> 01:58:09.445
like the weight of that is tremendous.

3090
01:58:09.445 --> 01:58:11.504
And when you let that go and let somebody in,

3091
01:58:11.504 --> 01:58:14.445
there's a huge release and the intimacy

3092
01:58:14.445 --> 01:58:17.362
that comes with that is tremendous.

3093
01:58:18.215 --> 01:58:22.457
The other thing I would suggest is in these exchanges

3094
01:58:22.457 --> 01:58:23.706
or in this dynamic to always,

3095
01:58:23.706 --> 01:58:25.446
this is something I do all the time

3096
01:58:25.446 --> 01:58:26.769
and I do it on the podcast,

3097
01:58:26.769 --> 01:58:29.264
is to lead with vulnerability.

3098
01:58:29.264 --> 01:58:30.411
Like if you,

3099
01:58:30.411 --> 01:58:32.314
instead of waiting for that person

3100
01:58:32.314 --> 01:58:35.540
to give you the feedback or to say the intimate thing,

3101
01:58:35.540 --> 01:58:37.954
like you've got to go first.

3102
01:58:37.954 --> 01:58:39.428
And I think when you do that,

3103
01:58:39.428 --> 01:58:42.297
you're giving the other permission

3104
01:58:42.297 --> 01:58:43.957
for that level of intimacy.

3105
01:58:43.957 --> 01:58:45.609
You're saying this is safe.

3106
01:58:45.609 --> 01:58:46.920
I trust you.

3107
01:58:46.920 --> 01:58:48.605
You can trust me.

3108
01:58:48.605 --> 01:58:49.874
And then with that,

3109
01:58:49.874 --> 01:58:51.947
it's practicing how to listen.

3110
01:58:51.947 --> 01:58:53.662
Like really listen,

3111
01:58:53.662 --> 01:58:54.968
because the most valuable thing

3112
01:58:54.968 --> 01:58:56.779
that you can give another person is your time

3113
01:58:56.779 --> 01:58:59.255
and of course your full attention.

3114
01:58:59.255 --> 01:59:01.549
And the more that the other person

3115
01:59:01.549 --> 01:59:03.949
really feels like they're being heard,

3116
01:59:03.949 --> 01:59:07.025
then the closer they're going to feel to you,

3117
01:59:07.025 --> 01:59:09.670
and the more they're gonna gravitate towards you.

3118
01:59:09.670 --> 01:59:12.128
Staying out of the other person's reaction

3119
01:59:12.128 --> 01:59:14.781
to your attempts at intimacy, I think is important.

3120
01:59:14.781 --> 01:59:18.091
If you're wed to a certain result,

3121
01:59:18.091 --> 01:59:19.865
like I'm gonna have this conversation

3122
01:59:19.865 --> 01:59:21.663
and then this is gonna happen,

3123
01:59:21.663 --> 01:59:23.819
then you're setting yourself up for disappointment.

3124
01:59:23.819 --> 01:59:25.843
So it's not about the result.

3125
01:59:25.843 --> 01:59:29.967
It's just about engaging in the process of being open,

3126
01:59:29.967 --> 01:59:32.025
vulnerable, and intimate and trusting

3127
01:59:32.025 --> 01:59:35.466
that over time that's gonna breathe the intimacy

3128
01:59:35.466 --> 01:59:38.274
that you seek, but trust takes time.

3129
01:59:38.274 --> 01:59:40.686
So patience, I think is super important.

3130
01:59:40.686 --> 01:59:43.806
And then the esteem piece I think is super important.

3131
01:59:43.806 --> 01:59:46.369
And forgive me if you've heard me say this,

3132
01:59:46.369 --> 01:59:47.605
'cause I repeat it all the time,

3133
01:59:47.605 --> 01:59:50.953
but self esteem comes through performing esteemable acts,

3134
01:59:50.953 --> 01:59:54.770
whether it's on behalf of others or for yourself,

3135
01:59:54.770 --> 01:59:56.806
it applies to yourself as well.

3136
01:59:56.806 --> 01:59:59.978
So simple things like setting, healthy boundaries

3137
01:59:59.978 --> 02:00:02.550
and making time for those that you care about,

3138
02:00:02.550 --> 02:00:04.391
investing and helping other people

3139
02:00:04.391 --> 02:00:06.639
all will slowly open you up

3140
02:00:06.639 --> 02:00:09.907
and ground you a little bit better

3141
02:00:09.907 --> 02:00:11.576
and make you a healthier person

3142
02:00:11.576 --> 02:00:15.228
for your current and future relationships.

3143
02:00:15.228 --> 02:00:16.547
And then the final thing I would say,

3144
02:00:16.547 --> 02:00:18.710
sorry, do you wanna say something?

3145
02:00:18.710 --> 02:00:20.342
No, I'm just agreeing with you.

3146
02:00:20.342 --> 02:00:23.235
The final thing, and this is important too,

3147
02:00:23.235 --> 02:00:25.445
is to forgive yourself,

3148
02:00:25.445 --> 02:00:27.034
to like let it go

3149
02:00:27.034 --> 02:00:29.572
because there is this narrative about,

3150
02:00:29.572 --> 02:00:31.643
I'm somebody with self-esteem

3151
02:00:31.643 --> 02:00:33.983
and I don't like to be uncomfortable

3152
02:00:33.983 --> 02:00:35.255
and I'm afraid of this.

3153
02:00:35.255 --> 02:00:36.182
And I'm afraid of that.

3154
02:00:36.182 --> 02:00:38.564
You've got to rewire that neurology

3155
02:00:38.564 --> 02:00:40.992
and start telling yourself a new story.

3156
02:00:40.992 --> 02:00:41.858
Like in other words,

3157
02:00:41.858 --> 02:00:43.159
letting go of that story

3158
02:00:43.159 --> 02:00:46.673
and opening up to perhaps a new and better story.

3159
02:00:46.673 --> 02:00:48.291
And again, those pushups,

3160
02:00:48.291 --> 02:00:49.873
those little actions that you're taking

3161
02:00:49.873 --> 02:00:51.366
will help inform that,

3162
02:00:51.366 --> 02:00:54.912
but that story is likely hardwired

3163
02:00:54.912 --> 02:00:56.392
into you and pretty calcified.

